2.9 Singular solutions in elastostatics
2.9.1 The delta-function
In potential theory, it is often helpful to introduce point singularities such as point charges or dipoles in electrostatics or point masses in gravitation. In inviscid fluid dynamics it is also common to discuss singular solutions describing sources and vortices, in the latter of which the singularity is localised on a line rather than a point. As we shall see, such fundamental solutions are very useful building blocks for constructing more general solutions.


